meta {
  name: Assign Member Roles
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orgs/{{orgSlug}}/members/{{memberUserId}}/roles
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "roles": ["developer", "deployer"]
  }
}

docs {
  Replaces the active role set for a user in an organisation. OrgAdmin (own org) or PlatformAdmin.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required.
    2. user_id param must be a valid UUID — 404 if not found in the org.
    3. Each role in roles[] must be a known role value; unknown values return 422.
    4. Only PlatformAdmin may grant or revoke platform_admin or auditor — OrgAdmin gets 403. OrgAdmin may grant app_user.
    5. Roles in the request not currently held are granted (new RoleAssignment row).
    6. Roles currently held not in the request are revoked (revoked_at = now, row kept for audit).
    7. Write role.assigned to audit_logs.

  Valid roles: developer | auditor | deployer | cluster_admin | org_admin | platform_admin | app_user

  Responses:
    200 OK           — { id, email, display_name, roles }
    401 unauthorized — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden    — OrgAdmin targeting another org, or granting platform_admin without authority
    404 not_found    — org or user not found
    422 validation_failed — unknown role value
}
